Image prompt rules: describe only what IS visible; never use negations (no, without, not, lacking, absent) because the image model ignores them and draws the thing anyway; describe the replacement instead (e.g. "a smooth blank head with a single thin dark slit" rather than "no face"). Whatever the subject (person, creature, place, object, event or god), name at least two details particular to this world and its peoples (their materials, dress, craft, land or light) so the image shows this world rather than a generic stock scene, in the look the world itself calls for, whether grounded or fantastic. Describe the content, light and composition only; never name an artistic medium, art style, camera or lens, because the world's chosen image style is applied to every prompt separately.
